==Yoruba==

===Etymology 1===
Possibly related to {{cog|igl|ójí}}, perhaps a Proto-Yoruboid innovation as the religious and spiritual concept of {{l|yo|Orí}} developed, and cognates do not exist outside of the Yoruboid group. Cognate with {{cog|idd|erío}}, {{cog|ife|eríwo}} and {{cog|its|orígho}}. Some proposed derivations include {{inh|yo|alv-yrd-pro|*ó-ɗí}} or {{inh|yo|alv-yrd-pro|*ó-rí}}. Folk etymologies often attribute etymology to {{af|yo|o-|rí|t1=nominalizing prefix|id1=nominalizing prefix|t2=to see}}

====Pronunciation====
*{{yo-IPA|orí}}

====Noun====
{{yo-noun|orí}}

# [[head]], [[top]], [[leader]]
#: {{syn|yo|orígho}} {{q|Ìkálẹ̀}}
#:{{syn|yo|oígho}} {{q|Oǹdó}}
#:{{syn|yo|orúwo}} {{q|Ìjẹ̀bú}}
# {{lb|yo|Yoruba religion}} the [[metaphysical]] [[concept]] of one's [[spiritual]] [[intuition]], [[destiny]], and [[consciousness]], deified as a divinity, {{l|yo|Orí}}.

